WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.992
A lakehouse combines file storage with table-like access.

00:00:03.992 --> 00:00:07.087
Raw files may enter the lakehouse first.

00:00:07.087 --> 00:00:10.677
Curated outputs are often stored as Delta tables.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:15.832
Spark provides distributed compute over those data assets.

00:00:15.832 --> 00:00:19.272
Reports, notebooks, and models consume the prepared results.

00:00:19.272 --> 00:00:25.047
This layered thinking helps keep raw, cleaned, and analytical data separate.

00:00:25.047 --> 00:00:30.457
A lakehouse combines scalable file-based storage with table-management features.

00:00:30.457 --> 00:00:39.047
Delta-style tables add transaction logs, schema controls, and reliable table operations on top of object

00:00:39.047 --> 00:00:39.392
storage.

00:00:39.392 --> 00:00:45.387
Keep raw ingestion, cleaned data, and curated analytical tables conceptually separate so lineage remains

00:00:45.387 --> 00:00:47.108
clear.
